<template><div class="stack"><div class="split grow"><div class="col"><h2>Research achievements</h2><div class="steps"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Compact retouching representation</h3><p>Reported reconstruction: FiveK 28.5 dB; PPSD 28.2 dB.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Conditional candidate generation</h3><p>Image and history condition a continuous distribution with fixed inference weights.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Measured GPU inference</h3><p>39.735 ms for one query under the report’s benchmark settings.</p></div></article></div></div><div class="col"><h2>Lessons from the evidence</h2><div class="steps"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Accuracy is not enough</h3><p>Ablations reveal dependence on each input and weaknesses in historical pairing.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Coverage is not preference validation</h3><p>Best-of-K requires target access and cannot replace a user study.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Claims need run-level provenance</h3><p>A versioned implementation does not prove which split and checkpoint generated a result.</p></div></article></div></div></div><p class="note">XingTang Chen’s individual contribution is documented separately: presentation engineering, evidence organisation, delivery and report assistance.</p></div></template>
